  "scope": "Focused independent mathematical and pinned-source review of WRS1--WRS5. This certifies literal local/Taylor kernel transport, the joint dependent comparison-kernel identity, and actual built-point identification. WRS6--WRS10 and their selected whole-contract closure are outside this focused review.",
  "findings": [],
  "checks": [
    "WRS1 retains all seventeen LocalToGlobal2 fields, including arbitrary local level tuples, full good-index guards, coefficient-field algebraicity, and cmp_K; no zero-chain substitution or fullness premise on N is introduced.",
    "WRS2 preserves every KerT field and the actual kerEntC construction. The polynomial quotients, chosen sections, prS/prT, thAtW, unC zero convention, all four KerEntHyp clauses and LevFree guard depend only on retained data.",
    "WRS3 applies one map on the dependent sum (GatTies, LatCmp, TwForms, KerFam), so both the local lattice field and comparison indices are transported before the kernel equality is used.",
    "WRS4 uses the Built witness col, ker0, ker_eq, ker, lev and errX. Its JoinTiedS, symmetric kernel embedding and positive-place clauses are on the supplied Extra kernel; the full five-field GroupCompatibility record is inherited exactly from GCF16.",
    "WRS5 matches positionOf, BPt.Y/hY/p, the exact nPrime span and hExpl6 depth, Obj.ofPt and ofObj transport. The p.Gy_eq substitution preserves the whole actual kernel domain, not only the comparison map.",
    "All coefficient fields, prime guards, arbitrary N/h and original class assumptions are unchanged. No WPt/RecT selector, nonempty family assertion, or unused EntC hypothesis is inserted into the built-object compatibility supplier."
  ],
